      ":question/problem": "![](images/b8/b8874b14fa80881e69cb1daee180d2e342a27c5902e66fc75d43622278176b09.png)\n\nConsider the square region $\u0394$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\n\u0394=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le \\sqrt{2},\\,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\le v\\le \\frac{\\pi }{3}\\},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (u\\operatorname{cos}\u2061v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}\u2061v).\n$$\n\nThe image of the bottom side of $\u0394$ under the action of $T$ is a line segment. Which of the following statements are true regarding the image?\n\nI. The image makes the angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ with the positive $x$-axis.\n\nII. The image makes the angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ with the positive $x$-axis.\n\nIII. The endpoints of the image lie on the circles of radii $1$ and $2$ centered at $O.$"
